# tally 2.1.8 P42, L §4.3 (B3 of group 4's review, agent/law_via_at): an ask's law expression reaches defs through
# their reads, but a def with its own written at (fixed, at fixday) reads at that date, so the chain stops there and
# cutoff_r's at reader is read at fixday: q is 1 at law date 2026-04-01, as at tally 2.1.7. 807e51d6 refused the
# file, LOAD-LAWDATE.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input cutoff: date
input fixday: date

def cutoff_r: date at reader
  rule base = cutoff

def fixed: date at fixday
  rule base = cutoff_r

def amount: num at reader
  rule base = 1

ask q: amount law fixed
ask q2: fixed

version v0
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  fixday = 2026-03-01 "s"

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-01
  cutoff = 2026-04-01 "s"
=== expect
q: 1
  law date 2026-04-01, cut 2026-06-10
q2: 2026-04-01
  cut 2026-06-10
